From: Balázs Gyimesi <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: qualcomm: rmnet: preset the flow hash of deaggregated packets

RPS asks every packet for its flow hash before it looks at the CPU map, so
a link whose RPS mask holds one CPU still pays for dissecting the headers
and siphashing them, about 2 % of the samples in a forwarding profile, and
the result chooses nothing. Give the deaggregated copy a fixed software hash
so skb_get_hash() returns at once. deagg_preset_hash=0 restores the old
behaviour, for a link that spreads over several CPUs.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_map_data.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_map_data.c
@@ -84,6 +84,15 @@
 	return alloc_skb(max_t(u32, len, min_alloc), GFP_ATOMIC);
 }
 
+/* The QMAP links steer to a single CPU, so the flow hash RPS asks for chooses
+ * nothing, yet dissecting the headers and siphashing them is paid per packet
+ * in get_rps_cpu(). A software hash set here skips both. Nothing else on this
+ * path reads it: the offload engine and the stack hash on their own terms.
+ */
+static bool rmnet_deagg_preset_hash = true;
+module_param_named(deagg_preset_hash, rmnet_deagg_preset_hash, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(deagg_preset_hash, "give deaggregated packets a fixed software flow hash, for links that steer to one CPU");
+
 static __sum16 *rmnet_map_get_csum_field(unsigned char protocol,
 					 const void *txporthdr)
 {
@@ -461,6 +470,9 @@
 	if (!skbn)
 		return NULL;
 
+	if (READ_ONCE(rmnet_deagg_preset_hash))
+		__skb_set_sw_hash(skbn, 1, false);
+
 	skbn->dev = skb->dev;
 	skb_reserve(skbn, RMNET_MAP_DEAGGR_HEADROOM);
 	skb_put(skbn, packet_len);
